# Optional per-user env file for the dev container. Copy to .devcontainer/.env (gitignored).
#
# Docker Compose auto-loads .devcontainer/.env and substitutes these values into docker-compose.yml.
# Values are NOT injected into the container automatically — docker-compose.yml forwards the ones it
# needs explicitly (currently GH_TOKEN, via its `environment:` block).
#
# Everything here is optional; the container starts fine without this file.

# Nothing here is about tool credentials: gh and Claude Code are both signed into from inside the
# container once (`gh auth login`, `claude`), and their config volumes keep that login across
# rebuilds. See README.md.

# --- Worktree mode (parallel agents) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Mount the project root (one level above this clone) at /workspaces so that `git worktree add`ed
# siblings (/workspaces/<branch>) are real host directories, visible from the host and persistent
# across rebuilds. Requires the on-disk layout described in README.md:
#
#   <project-root>/               <- mounted at /workspaces
#     open_cine_prod_tools/       <- this clone; opened in VS Code; lands at
#                                    /workspaces/open_cine_prod_tools
#     <some-branch>/              <- `git worktree add`ed siblings, land at /workspaces/<some-branch>
#
# To enable worktree mode, uncomment both lines below:
#
# WORKSPACE_MOUNT_SOURCE=../..
# WORKSPACE_MOUNT_TARGET=/workspaces
